name: files
boss: CopyPasta
flavor: Every copy is a ghost of the original.
brief: Six commands move bytes around: cp copies, mv renames or moves, rm
brief: deletes, mkdir and rmdir make and unmake directories, touch creates an
brief: empty file or bumps its timestamp.
brief:
brief: Two of them are quietly dangerous. cp and mv overwrite the destination
brief: without asking. -n refuses to, -i asks first. Learn those two flags now
brief: and you will not need to learn them from a loss later.
---
q: {copy @cfg@ to @cfg2@|make a copy of @cfg@ named @cfg2@|duplicate @cfg@ as @cfg2@}
a: cp @cfg@ @cfg2@
state: exists:@cfg2@
ref: cp
teach: cp
hint: just cp, then the source, then the destination
---
q: {copy @txt@ into the @dir@ directory, keeping its name|put a copy of @txt@ inside @dir@ with the same name|copy @txt@ into @dir@ without renaming it}, with cp
a: cp @txt@ @dir@/
a: cp @txt@ @dir@
state: exists:@dir@/@txt@
ref: cp
teach: cp
hint: when the destination is a directory, cp keeps the original name for you
---
q: {copy @dir@ and everything inside it to @dir2@-copy|copy @dir@ and all its contents to @dir2@-copy|duplicate @dir@, contents included, as @dir2@-copy}, with cp
a: cp -r @dir@ @dir2@-copy
a: cp -R @dir@ @dir2@-copy
a: cp -a @dir@ @dir2@-copy
state: exists:@dir2@-copy
ref: cp
teach: cp -r
hint: the flag cp calls "Recurse"
---
q: {don't overwrite @cfg2@ -- cp @cfg@ there only if missing|duplicate @cfg@ as @cfg2@ with cp, skipping one that exists|cp @cfg@ to @cfg2@ only if @cfg2@ is missing}
a: cp -n @cfg@ @cfg2@
why: primitive-cost
ref: cp
teach: cp -n
hint: n for "no clobber"
---
q: {cp @txt@ to @txt@.bak, keeping timestamps and permissions|cp @txt@ to @txt@.bak without losing timestamps or permissions|back up @txt@ to @txt@.bak with cp, keeping timestamps intact}
a: cp -p @txt@ @txt@.bak
a: cp -a @txt@ @txt@.bak
state: exists:@txt@.bak
ref: cp
teach: cp -p
hint: p for preserve
---
q: {cp @dir@ to @dir2@-archive preserving everything, one flag only|cp @dir@ to @dir2@-archive keeping it all intact, single flag|archive-copy @dir@ to @dir2@-archive with cp, everything in one flag}
a: cp -a @dir@ @dir2@-archive
state: exists:@dir2@-archive
ref: cp
teach: cp -a
hint: cp calls it "Same as -dpR"
---
q: {rename @txt@ to @word@.txt|change @txt@'s name to @word@.txt|give @txt@ the new name @word@.txt}
a: mv @txt@ @word@.txt
state: exists:@word@.txt
ref: mv
teach: mv
hint: mv renames when the destination isn't a directory
---
q: {move @cfg@ into @dir@/|relocate @cfg@ into the @dir@ directory|put @cfg@ inside @dir@}
a: mv @cfg@ @dir@/
a: mv @cfg@ @dir@
state: exists:@dir@/@cfg@
ref: mv
teach: mv
hint: same command as renaming -- the destination just happens to be a directory
---
q: {mv @txt@ to @dir@/, but never overwrite a file already there|mv @txt@ into @dir@ without clobbering anything already there|relocate @txt@ to @dir@ with mv, refusing a name already taken}
a: mv -n @txt@ @dir@/
a: mv -n @txt@ @dir@
state: exists:@dir@/@txt@
ref: mv
teach: mv -n
hint: n for no-clobber, same idea as cp -n
---
q: {delete @txt@|remove @txt@|get rid of @txt@}
a: rm @txt@
state: gone:@txt@
ref: rm
teach: rm
hint: just rm and the filename -- no flags for a plain file
---
q: {delete @dir@ and everything inside it|remove @dir@ along with everything it contains|wipe out @dir@ and its contents}, with rm
a: rm -r @dir@
a: rm -rf @dir@
state: gone:@dir@
ref: rm
teach: rm -r
hint: r for recursive -- required before rm will touch a directory's contents
---
q: {delete @txt@ without complaining if it is already gone|remove @txt@ silently even if it doesn't exist|delete @txt@, staying quiet if it's already missing}, with rm
a: rm -f @txt@
state: gone:@txt@
ref: rm
teach: rm -f
hint: f for force -- it also silences the "no such file" error
---
q: %make% a directory called @word@
a: mkdir @word@
state: exists:@word@
ref: mkdir
teach: mkdir
hint: just mkdir and the name -- no flags needed
---
q: %make% @dir@/@word@/deep with mkdir, making the missing parents too
a: mkdir -p @dir@/@word@/deep
state: exists:@dir@/@word@/deep
ref: mkdir
teach: mkdir -p
hint: p for parents
---
q: %make% a directory @word@, only you can enter, with mkdir's numeric mode
a: mkdir -m 700 @word@
state: exists:@word@
ref: mkdir
teach: mkdir -m
hint: -m sets permissions at creation time -- 700 is owner-only rwx
---
q: {remove the already-empty directory empty-dir|delete empty-dir, which is already empty|get rid of empty-dir, sitting there empty}
a: rmdir empty-dir
state: gone:empty-dir
ref: rmdir
teach: rmdir
hint: rmdir only works when the directory is empty -- rm -r doesn't care
---
q: %make% an empty file called @word@.txt
a: touch @word@.txt
a: > @word@.txt
state: exists:@word@.txt
ref: touch
teach: touch
hint: touch creates it if missing, or just bumps its timestamp if it exists
---
q: {update the timestamp on @txt@ to now, without changing its contents|bump @txt@'s modification time to now, leaving its contents alone|refresh @txt@'s timestamp without touching what's inside it}
a: touch @txt@
state: match:@txt@:rotate
ref: touch
teach: touch
hint: with no flags, touch just sets the timestamp to now
---
q: {touch @txt@ but do NOT create it if it is missing|touch @txt@, but skip creating it if it doesn't exist|refresh @txt@'s timestamp with touch, only if it already exists}
a: touch -c @txt@
why: primitive-cost
ref: touch
teach: touch -c
hint: c stops touch from creating the file when it doesn't exist
---
q: %make% a symbolic link @word@-link to @txt@, with ln
a: ln -s @txt@ @word@-link
state: exists:@word@-link
ref: ln
teach: ln -s
hint: s for symbolic; without it you get a hard link
---
q: %make% a hard link called @word@-hard to @txt@
a: ln @txt@ @word@-hard
state: exists:@word@-hard
ref: ln
teach: ln
hint: no flag needed -- ln makes a hard link by default
---
q: %make% symlink @word@-link to @txt@ with ln, replacing any there
a: ln -sf @txt@ @word@-link
state: exists:@word@-link
ref: ln
teach: ln -f
hint: combine -s for symbolic with -f to replace what's already there
---
q: {ask with cp before copying @cfg@ over an existing @cfg2@|cp @cfg@ as @cfg2@, asking first if it'd overwrite|cp @cfg@ over @cfg2@, confirming before any overwrite}
a: cp -i @cfg@ @cfg2@
why: interactive
ref: cp
teach: cp -i
hint: i for interactive -- prompts before clobbering
---
q: {cp @cfg@ onto @cfg2@, deleting it first if the write fails|cp @cfg@ onto @cfg2@, removing it if it won't take a write|force cp of @cfg@ onto @cfg2@, deleting it if the write fails}
a: cp -f @cfg@ @cfg2@
state: exists:@cfg2@
ref: cp
teach: cp -f
hint: f removes the destination first if a plain overwrite would fail
---
q: {mv @txt@ to @word@.txt, asking first if it would overwrite|rename @txt@ to @word@.txt with mv, but prompt before overwrite|before renaming @txt@ to @word@.txt with mv, confirm any clobber}
a: mv -i @txt@ @word@.txt
why: interactive
ref: mv
teach: mv -i
hint: i for interactive, same idea as cp -i
---
q: {mv @txt@ to @word@.txt, forcing it with no prompt|rename @txt@ to @word@.txt with mv, overwriting with no confirm|force the mv of @txt@ to @word@.txt, skip the prompt}
a: mv -f @txt@ @word@.txt
state: exists:@word@.txt
ref: mv
teach: mv -f
hint: f skips confirmation -- the opposite of -i
---
q: {delete @txt@ but ask for confirmation first|remove @txt@, prompting for confirmation first|delete @txt@ only after you confirm it}, with rm
a: rm -i @txt@
why: interactive
ref: rm
teach: rm -i
hint: i for interactive -- prompts before removing
---
q: {remove prune/mid/deep and any parents left empty, with rmdir|delete prune/mid/deep, cleaning up now-empty parents, with rmdir|rmdir removes prune/mid/deep and the empty parents it leaves}
a: rmdir -p prune/mid/deep
state: gone:prune
ref: rmdir
teach: rmdir -p
hint: p walks back up removing each parent as long as it's now empty
---
q: %make% @word@.fifo, a pipe so two processes can talk directly
a: mkfifo @word@.fifo
state: exists:@word@.fifo
ref: mkfifo
teach: mkfifo
hint: a fifo connects a writer to a reader instead of storing data
---
q: %make% a named pipe @word@.fifo with mkfifo, readable/writable by you only
a: mkfifo -m 600 @word@.fifo
state: exists:@word@.fifo
ref: mkfifo
teach: mkfifo -m
hint: -m sets permissions at creation, same as mkdir -m
---
q: %make% a temporary file with a name nothing else will collide with
a: mktemp
why: primitive-cost
ref: mktemp
teach: mktemp
hint: generates and creates a uniquely-named file, then prints its path
---
q: %make% a temporary directory with mktemp, not a temporary file
a: mktemp -d
why: primitive-cost
ref: mktemp
teach: mktemp -d
hint: d for directory instead of a file
---
q: get a temporary name from mktemp without actually creating anything
a: mktemp -u
why: primitive-cost
ref: mktemp
teach: mktemp -u
hint: u for unsafe -- hands you a name without reserving it, so something else could grab it first
